# Code documentation

Applies when editing **code** under the globs (not product copy in i18n catalogs alone).

**If a competent developer can understand it from the code, do not document it. Document WHY, invariants, security, and Discord constraints.**

- Code explains WHAT; comments explain WHY.
- English only in the engineering codebase (comments, JSDoc, module READMEs, TODOs).
- User-facing content: en + pl via [friends-i18n.mdc](./friends-i18n.mdc).
- Do not duplicate Prisma / DTO / i18n as a second source of truth.
- Update or delete stale comments in the same change.

Module README = architecture map, not a file inventory. Known: `apps/api/README.md`, `apps/activity/README.md`, `packages/db/README.md`.
